  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14093691",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-128382",
      "knowledge_point_id": "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Vector Equation of a Plane Given Its Cartesian Equation",
      "problem": "Given the Cartesian equation $3x+5y+15=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨3,5,0⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+5y+15 & =0 \\\\ 5y & =-3x-15 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{5}x-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$, we get $y=-3.$ Hence, the point $P(0,-3,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,-3,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,-3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨3,5,0⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(r-⟨0,3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨3,5,-1⟩=0",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(r-⟨0,-3,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨3,5,0⟩=0",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(r-⟨0,-3,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨3,0,5⟩=0",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(r-⟨0,0,-3⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,3,0⟩=0",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "(r-⟨0,0,3⟩)\\cdot ⟨5,3,0⟩=0",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_answer_policy": {
