  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14093719",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-74650",
      "knowledge_point_id": "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Value of a Constant for Which a Given Linear System Is Consistent or Inconsistent",
      "problem": "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+6y=4 \\\\  & x+(k+1)y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & k+1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & k+1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & k-2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+6y=4 \\\\  & (k-2)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=2,$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y.$ So, we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $2x+6y=4.$  \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=2.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "k=-2",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "k=\\frac{1}{2}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "k=-\\frac{1}{2}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "k=2",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "k=-4",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_answer_policy": {
